{
  "$comment": [
    "File moves for the parity gate (20-M5-plan.md WP-0 / WP-2 / WP-3).",
    "Each entry maps a baseline path to where it lives now: {\"from\": \"verification/x.mjs\", \"to\": \"verification/y.mjs\"}.",
    "A split lists every part: {\"from\": \"a.mjs\", \"to\": [\"b.mjs\", \"c.mjs\"]}; the parts must add up to the original.",
    "Without an entry a move reads as a deletion and check:parity fails. Entries stay after --write records the new paths;",
    "a from that is no longer in the baseline is simply inert.",
    "A suite split lists the parts a baseline suite became; their union must carry every file and the same assertion count.",
    "A split whose from is no longer in the baseline is inert, exactly like a move whose from is no longer in the closure.",
    "WP-5b: a split that keeps its original path and only adds sibling parts needs no entry here; the gate sees the original plus the added parts inside the same suite closure, and the suite total is compared as a whole."
  ],
